  "statement": "\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUse your calculator to find the greatest common factor (GCF) of 456, 792, and 1002.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e",
  "statementFigure": null,
  "question": null,
  "widgetSlot": null,
  "steps": [
    {
      "role": "hint",
      "content": "\u003cdiv class\u003d\"step_content\"\u003e\n \u003cp\u003ePress \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_16915\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/qmath.gif\" onmouseout\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOut()\" onmouseover\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOver(\u0026quot;token_16915\u0026quot;,180)\"\u003e and select \u003cb\u003egcd(\u003c/b\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e",
      "figure": null,
      "figures": null
    },
    {
      "role": "step",
      "content": "\u003cdiv class\u003d\"step_content\"\u003e\n \u003cp\u003ePress \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_16916\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/qmath.gif\" onmouseout\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOut()\" onmouseover\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOver(\u0026quot;token_16916\u0026quot;,180)\"\u003e and press \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_16917\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/q2.gif\"\u003e to select \u003cb\u003egcd(\u003c/b\u003e. (This stands for \"greatest common denominator\", but works the same way as GCF).\u003c/p\u003e\n \u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\u003cimg class\u003d\"graphimgstatic id\u003d\" figure-1 src\u003d\"/modules/gcprealgpractice/gcprealgpractice_3_1_numbertheory_2_20/f-20-2-1.gif\"\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e",
      "figure": null,
      "figures": null
    },
    {
      "role": "hint",
      "content": "\u003cdiv class\u003d\"step_content\"\u003e\n \u003cp\u003eYour calculator can only find the GCF of two numbers at a time.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e",
      "figure": null,
      "figures": null
    },
    {
      "role": "step",
      "content": "\u003cdiv class\u003d\"step_content\"\u003e\n \u003cp\u003eUnfortunately, your calculator can only find the GCF of two numbers at a time. So, first find the GCF of the first two, then find the GCF of this answer and the third number.\u003c/p\u003e\n \u003cp\u003eEnter the first two numbers, separated by a comma. Press \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_16918\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/q4.gif\"\u003e \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_16919\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/q5.gif\"\u003e \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_16920\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/q6.gif\"\u003e \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_16921\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/qcomma.gif\" onmouseout\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOut()\" onmouseover\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOver(\u0026quot;token_16921\u0026quot;,125)\"\u003e \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_16922\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/q7.gif\"\u003e \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_16923\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/q9.gif\"\u003e \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_16924\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/q2.gif\"\u003e \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_16925\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/qcloseparen.gif\" onmouseout\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOut()\" onmouseover\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOver(\u0026quot;token_16925\u0026quot;,121)\"\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n \u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\u003cimg class\u003d\"graphimgstatic id\u003d\" figure-3 src\u003d\"/modules/gcprealgpractice/gcprealgpractice_3_1_numbertheory_2_20/f-20-2-2.gif\"\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e",
      "figure": null,
      "figures": null
    },
    {
      "role": "hint",
      "content": "\u003cdiv class\u003d\"step_content\"\u003e\n \u003cp\u003ePress \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_16926\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/qenter.gif\" onmouseout\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOut()\" onmouseover\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOver(\u0026quot;token_16926\u0026quot;,144)\"\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e",
      "figure": null,
      "figures": null
    },
    {
      "role": "step",
      "content": "\u003cdiv class\u003d\"step_content\"\u003e\n \u003cp\u003ePress \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_16927\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/qenter.gif\" onmouseout\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOut()\" onmouseover\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOver(\u0026quot;token_16927\u0026quot;,144)\"\u003e. The calculator gives the GCF as 24.\u003c/p\u003e\n \u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\u003cimg class\u003d\"graphimgstatic id\u003d\" figure-5 src\u003d\"/modules/gcprealgpractice/gcprealgpractice_3_1_numbertheory_2_20/f-20-2-3.gif\"\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e",
      "figure": null,
      "figures": null
    },
    {
      "role": "hint",
      "content": "\u003cdiv class\u003d\"step_content\"\u003e\n \u003cp\u003eNow find the GCF of 24 and 1002.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e",
      "figure": null,
      "figures": null
    },
    {
      "role": "step",
      "content": "\u003cdiv class\u003d\"step_content\"\u003e\n \u003cp\u003eNow find the GCF of 24 and 1002.\u003c/p\u003e\n \u003cp\u003ePress \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_16928\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/qmath.gif\" onmouseout\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOut()\" onmouseover\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOver(\u0026quot;token_16928\u0026quot;,180)\"\u003e and press \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_16929\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/q2.gif\"\u003e to select \u003cb\u003egcd(\u003c/b\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n \u003cp\u003eThen press \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_16930\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/q2.gif\"\u003e \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_16931\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/q4.gif\"\u003e \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_16932\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/qcomma.gif\" onmouseout\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOut()\" onmouseover\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOver(\u0026quot;token_16932\u0026quot;,125)\"\u003e \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_16933\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/q1.gif\"\u003e \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_16934\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/q0.gif\"\u003e \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_16935\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/q0.gif\"\u003e \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_16936\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/q2.gif\"\u003e \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_16937\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/qcloseparen.gif\" onmouseout\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOut()\" onmouseover\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOver(\u0026quot;token_16937\u0026quot;,121)\"\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n \u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\u003cimg class\u003d\"graphimgstatic id\u003d\" figure-7 src\u003d\"/modules/gcprealgpractice/gcprealgpractice_3_1_numbertheory_2_20/f-20-2-4.gif\"\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e",
      "figure": null,
      "figures": null
    },
    {
      "role": "hint",
      "content": "\u003cdiv class\u003d\"step_content\"\u003e\n \u003cp\u003ePress \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_16938\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/qenter.gif\" onmouseout\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOut()\" onmouseover\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOver(\u0026quot;token_16938\u0026quot;,144)\"\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e",
      "figure": null,
      "figures": null
    },
    {
      "role": "step",
      "content": "\u003cdiv class\u003d\"step_content\"\u003e\n \u003cp\u003ePress \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_16939\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/qenter.gif\" onmouseout\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOut()\" onmouseover\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOver(\u0026quot;token_16939\u0026quot;,144)\"\u003e. The calculator gives the GCF as 6.\u003c/p\u003e\n \u003cp\u003eSo, the GCF of 456, 792, and 1002 is 6.\u003c/p\u003e\n \u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n \u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\u003cimg class\u003d\"graphimgstatic id\u003d\" figure-9 src\u003d\"/modules/gcprealgpractice/gcprealgpractice_3_1_numbertheory_2_20/f-20-2-5.gif\"\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e",
